<title>BELGIUM: Belgium raises liquidity at money tender.</title>
<headline>Belgium raises liquidity at money tender.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank raised money market liquidity at its fixed-rate tender for seven-day advances. Details -</p>
<p>    Value date 07/05	  expiry on 14/05    NBVA</p>
<p>    Amount allotted	   20.000 bln bfr    (15.000 bln *)</p>
<p>    Interest rate	     3.00 pct	    (3.00 pct **)</p>
<p>    Total amount of bids    108.350 bln bfr</p>
<p>Percentage of bids accepted  18.28</p>
<p>*  amount draining from the money market on 07/05</p>
<p>** interest rate at previous tender on 28/04</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
